<%-- "Create Idea" popup (Reviews -> Idea Review & Planning screen only) - opened by the
     "+ Create Idea" button in reviews-content.jspf's tab header row. Reuses the exact same Submit
     Idea form fragment (fragments/idea-submit-form.jspf), fields, client validation
     (idea-submit.js) and backend endpoint/logic (IdeaMvcController#submit / IdeaService#submit) as
     the full-page /app/ideas/new screen - this is presentation only, never a second/parallel Idea
     submission implementation. Same permission rule as Submit Idea itself: IdeaService#submit has
     no authority check beyond being logged in, so this button/modal is available to every viewer
     who can reach the Reviews screen at all, matching the "Submit Idea" nav link's own reach
     (visible unconditionally to every authenticated Access Class in fragments/nav.jsp). --%>
<div class="kcpc-modal-overlay hidden" id="ideaCreateModalOverlay">
    <div class="kcpc-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="ideaCreateModalTitle">
        <div class="kcpc-modal-header">
            <h3 id="ideaCreateModalTitle">Submit an Idea</h3>
            <button type="button" class="kcpc-modal-close" id="ideaCreateModalClose" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
        </div>
        <div class="kcpc-modal-body">
            <c:set var="ideaSubmitFormAjax" value="${true}"/>
            <%@ include file="idea-submit-form.jspf" %>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
